\ Verify the unary inline PIC fast path fires for `inspect`.
\ `.` is `[ inspect print-line ]`; `inspect` is a unary generic native
\ (value -- string). Before the unary sibling of emitInlinePicCheck existed,
\ its call site always routed through the plain native fallback. Running `.`
\ on fixnums seeds the interpreter PIC with the fixnum type, so the frozen
\ snapshot drives an inline unary check for fixnum.

double: ( n -- n ) [ 2 * ] ;

